// `kinds` names the family first and the semantic kind second: `KeywordAction`
// is the declaration's identity, `Instruction` the position its body occupies,
// so a keyword action resolves where a card writes an instruction.
//
// A declaration file writes its action's instruction (`body`) and never who
// performs it: that is the actor, the controller unless a handoff
// (`act(player, …)`) names another player (ADR 7, ruling 2026-10-05). The
// body here is the record of what the file wrote, and
// `deckmaste_semantics_v2::keywords` builds the action's definition from it:
// `Enact(verb: <deed>, instruction: <body>, agent: Some(Actor))`, where the
// deed is `Action(<label>)`, the label the words the name spells, unless the
// file writes `deed`. `deed: None` leaves the instruction unwrapped, and a
// declaration with no body stays bodyless. A file may write `agent: None`,
// and nothing else there, for a deed the checker gives no player performer
// (Lean `actFacts`, `enactAgentOk`): the wrapper then records none.
(
    name: "KeywordAction",
    kinds: [Macro],
    params: {
        "name": String,
        "params": Elidable(Any),
        "spelling": String,
        "grammar": Elidable(Any),
        "deed": Elidable(Any),
        "agent": Elidable(Any),
        "body": Default(Any, ()),
    },
    body: (
        name: Param(name),
        kinds: [KeywordAction, Instruction],
        params: Param(params),
        metadata: (
            spelling: Param(spelling),
            grammar: Param(grammar),
        ),
        body: (deed: Param(deed), agent: Param(agent), instruction: Param(body)),
    ),
)
